    "conventions": "Vietnamese names run family name, middle name, given name: Nguyễn Văn Hùng, Trần Thị Lan. About four in ten people are Nguyễn, and Trần, Lê, Phạm, Hoàng (Huỳnh in the south), Vũ (Võ in the south) and Phan are next, so people are called by the LAST part, the given name, never the family name: Hùng, Lan. The middle name was traditionally Văn for men and Thị for women; today it is usually a chosen word that pairs with the given name (Minh Anh, Đức Anh, Ngọc Anh), so the given lists here hold middle and given name together. In speech a name always comes with a kinship word by age: anh (older man), chị (older woman), em (younger), cô and chú (aunt and uncle age), bác (older still). Hoa families, Vietnamese of Chinese descent, mostly in Chợ Lớn, use Vietnamese readings of Chinese surnames such as Lâm, Trương, Quách and Diệp.",
